true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T10:25:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/christopherdebeer/workspace/commit/0487fd62e5868ba0b3b144a3c555ab10fbdb96bf","node_id":"C_kwDOORTQmNoAKDA0ODdmZDYyZTU4NjhiYTBiM2IxNDRhM2M1NTVhYjEwZmJkYjk2YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/christopherdebeer/workspace/commit/4eb39c9c6482ffd8f8ec4035541d52f993cbedc5","sha":"4eb39c9c6482ffd8f8ec4035541d52f993cbedc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/4eb39c9c6482ffd8f8ec4035541d52f993cbedc5"}],"sha":"0487fd62e5868ba0b3b144a3c555ab10fbdb96bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/0487fd62e5868ba0b3b144a3c555ab10fbdb96bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/4eb39c9c6482ffd8f8ec4035541d52f993cbedc5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T10:24:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T10:24:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"stillwater: the maths revised — the right question, clearly, at the right time\n\nKeeps the relationship work (missing numbers, inverses, equality both ways,\nanswers the dew can hold, no timers) and reworks how it is paced and shown:\n\n- The question is one clear line at the top, as large as the counting\n  numeral, its blank filling with the dew gathered. Under it, while a skill\n  is new, a dot picture (a whole in fives; an array for equal groups; rings\n  holding the group size for ÷) that lights as dew is gathered and fades as\n  the skill is learned. No instruction line, no word toolbar, no error\n  sentences: too much shakes the blank and the last leaf is let go.\n- Help is two small marks: a speaker (the question read aloud, the picture\n  shown; again, and it is worked through with its own numbers, aloud) and\n  another question.\n- No child-facing level menu. Hold the title for a grown-ups'' panel: the\n  school year sets a starting level and a floor (?year=N, ?maths=N).\n- Levels in national-curriculum / ready-to-progress order: counting, facts\n  within 10, within 20, 2/5/10 tables, tens and ones, 3/4/8 tables, tables\n  to 12, connections. Moving on needs three clean in a row per skill on two\n  different days; a level not holding steps back one.\n- Forms and numbers grow with the child inside a level (unknown at the end,\n  then anywhere, then the equation turned round; ranges widen).\n- Times questions are equal groups gathered as leaves that match (3 × 5 =\n  three leaves of five), never a remainder in disguise; larger facts ask a\n  group size. Dew condenses as matching leaves plus a decoy or two.\n- Relationship answers go into the fact memory and stretch like counting:\n  due facts come back, relief reviews the level before, finales still come.\n- New skills arrive in teaching order.\n\nTests: tests/stillwater-challenges.test.ts (new); the fluency test now\nmatches the untimed quality; the cell''s challenges.test.cjs follows the API.\nDocs: MATHS-REVIEW \"Revision\"; REVIEW rounds 64–66.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XpPcniK77FYo3hrbH4MFqQ","tree":{"sha":"2c5a8a29d495371defe5f79cd8ac8597c369fcc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/trees/2c5a8a29d495371defe5f79cd8ac8597c369fcc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/commits/4eb39c9c6482ffd8f8ec4035541d52f993cbedc5","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c5a8a29d495371defe5f79cd8ac8597c369fcc3\nparent f9d80cdd0867bfd463652ea9ebc17703339bc00d\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790763890 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790763890 +0000\n\nstillwater: the maths revised — the right question, clearly, at the right time\n\nKeeps the relationship work (missing numbers, inverses, equality both ways,\nanswers the dew can hold, no timers) and reworks how it is paced and shown:\n\n- The question is one clear line at the top, as large as the counting\n  numeral, its blank filling with the dew gathered. Under it, while a skill\n  is new, a dot picture (a whole in fives; an array for equal groups; rings\n  holding the group size for ÷) that lights as dew is gathered and fades as\n  the skill is learned. No instruction line, no word toolbar, no error\n  sentences: too much shakes the blank and the last leaf is let go.\n- Help is two small marks: a speaker (the question read aloud, the picture\n  shown; again, and it is worked through with its own numbers, aloud) and\n  another question.\n- No child-facing level menu. Hold the title for a grown-ups'' panel: the\n  school year sets a starting level and a floor (?year=N, ?maths=N).\n- Levels in national-curriculum / ready-to-progress order: counting, facts\n  within 10, within 20, 2/5/10 tables, tens and ones, 3/4/8 tables, tables\n  to 12, connections. Moving on needs three clean in a row per skill on two\n  different days; a level not holding steps back one.\n- Forms and numbers grow with the child inside a level (unknown at the end,\n  then anywhere, then the equation turned round; ranges widen).\n- Times questions are equal groups gathered as leaves that match (3 × 5 =\n  three leaves of five), never a remainder in disguise; larger facts ask a\n  group size. Dew condenses as matching leaves plus a decoy or two.\n- Relationship answers go into the fact memory and stretch like counting:\n  due facts come back, relief reviews the level before, finales still come.\n- New skills arrive in teaching order.\n\nTests: tests/stillwater-challenges.test.ts (new); the fluency test now\nmatches the untimed quality; the cell''s challenges.test.cjs follows the API.\nDocs: MATHS-REVIEW \"Revision\"; REVIEW rounds 64–66.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XpPcniK77FYo3hrbH4MFqQ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPmvGS5Q\nQxmKkF11RBYTzyTehRiz8WGqphuAazsh/XcN8plO