herdebeer/workspace/commits/360cc2da5a59b6faf4a23f85d6b4362e3e90c966"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/df48efbbd9ffe73a64518ec1afa1c4dfd41694c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:41:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:41:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"stillwater: water glyphs in each leaf''s own hand\n\nThe atlas no longer draws the glyphs: it holds only each one''s key shape,\nas the distance to its path (strokes merged with a smooth minimum, so\nwater fills the corners) and the distance along the stroke to a free end.\n\nThe hand is procedural in PAD_FS, seeded by the leaf: a lean, a slight\nturn and squash, a slow waver and a little tremor in the line, water\nthat swells and thins along it, pools here and there, beads at the ends,\nand a few stray drops near the strokes but clear of them. The shape\nmoves only a little, so it stays legible; the water on it is free to be\nmessy. The same leaf keeps its own hand.\n\n?glyphs=repeat&chars=37 fills the leaves near the middle of the view with\na few characters repeated, to see the variation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XpPcniK77FYo3hrbH4MFqQ","tree":{"sha":"89d7d9e4d57d5867181aa8a75f8f03f70e1a005c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/trees/89d7d9e4d57d5867181aa8a75f8f03f70e1a005c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/commits/df48efbbd9ffe73a64518ec1afa1c4dfd41694c8","verification":{"payload":"tree 89d7d9e4d57d5867181aa8a75f8f03f70e1a005c\nparent 412950d98547785ae435adea2f2928a5f45ef9f6\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790761285 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790761285 +0000\n\nstillwater: water glyphs in each leaf''s own hand\n\nThe atlas no longer draws the glyphs: it holds only each one''s key shape,\nas the distance to its path (strokes merged with a smooth minimum, so\nwater fills the corners) and the distance along the stroke to a free end.\n\nThe hand is procedural in PAD_FS, seeded by the leaf: a lean, a slight\nturn and squash, a slow waver and a little tremor in the line, water\nthat swells and thins along it, pools here and there, beads at the ends,\nand a few stray drops near the strokes but clear of them. The shape\nmoves only a little, so it stays legible; the water on it is free to be\nmessy. The same leaf keeps its own hand.\n\n?glyphs=repeat&chars=37 fills the leaves near the middle of the view with\na few characters repeated, to see the variation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XpPcniK77FYo3hrbH4MFqQ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD9m4AqM\n1S4qTvGZzeXDFxTg92Zzrz6WH3ORJmdDUu+bqdO7O/aE