here strokes meet and a few stray drops;\n  baked once into a 4×4 half-float atlas of height and slope.\n- PAD_FS lights a glyph the way the dew is lit: the leaf magnified across\n  the stroke, a dark contact line toward the sun and a thin bright one away\n  from it, sky only at the very edge, a sun streak along the stroke, the\n  lantern''s glint, light focused through it, a small shadow. Upright on\n  screen however the leaf turns. Carried in the drop texture (one entry,\n  z < 0), so no new instance data.\n- ?glyphs=1: a dewy leaf shows its count (1–9) as a numeral in water in\n  place of its drops; ?glyphs=half: every other leaf, to compare with dew;\n  ?glyphs=sheet: all sixteen on the leaves nearest the middle of the view.\n\nFound on the way: a rivulet''s highlight is a line, not a point, so the\ndew''s fwidth-sharpened pinpoint breaks into a 2×2 hatch on it; the glyph\nhighlights use a fixed, broader roughness instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XpPcniK77FYo3hrbH4MFqQ","tree":{"sha":"09a569d82517ad5c21c286b7416511efabb8b6da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/trees/09a569d82517ad5c21c286b7416511efabb8b6da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/commits/0e58ad7ce5506fd7c1b493b482f063274eb18347","verification":{"payload":"tree 09a569d82517ad5c21c286b7416511efabb8b6da\nparent f89d9698589b2b95301bc7fd5f41039166970b54\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790760531 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790760531 +0000\n\nstillwater: an experiment — numerals and signs drawn in water on the leaves\n\nBehind a flag; play is unchanged.\n\n- client/glyphs.ts: 0–9 + − × ÷ = ? as strokes a wet fingertip would take,\n  each stroke a rivulet (a round bead swept along it) with beaded ends, a\n  gentle waver, meniscus fillets where strokes meet and a few stray drops;\n  baked once into a 4×4 half-float atlas of height 