ub.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/a90f3200b0cae466028156561c9e6e30e796a72b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T01:08:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T01:08:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"playtest: two-step lookahead (harness h4), objective in the question; 15× faster hooks\n\n- runner: an option that makes no progress itself but enables a follow-up that\n  does (place a tile, then enter it; step towards an unvisited tile) is\n  labelled ''then …: → …'' — only when that follow-up isn''t already available.\n  Jev had shuttled between visited tiles; the judge put 70 % of the blame on\n  the players, not the rules.\n- the move question states the player''s secret objective and progress.\n- registry: getEnabledMechanics cached by the set of configured keys (it ran\n  on every hook call — ~60 % of engine CPU); simulation cost per decision\n  fell from ~0.57 s to ~0.04 s.\n- devtools/smoke.ts --sim: a free stand-in decider that exercises and times\n  the consequence simulation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011oR3V7hLncLCGgHh8wRUV4","tree":{"sha":"bc16cdabb3ed3aa57ec539fc926504d04d38762c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/trees/bc16cdabb3ed3aa57ec539fc926504d04d38762c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/commits/a90f3200b0cae466028156561c9e6e30e796a72b","verification":{"payload":"tree bc16cdabb3ed3aa57ec539fc926504d04d38762c\nparent 94fe7bff314e1c446d8ba47dea17b4bf29aaa612\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790730532 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790730532 +0000\n\nplaytest: two-step lookahead (harness h4), objective in the question; 15× faster hooks\n\n- runner: an option that makes no progress itself but enables a follow-up that\n  does (place a tile, then enter it; step towards an unvisited tile) is\n  labelled ''then …: → …'' — only when that follow-up isn''t already available.\n  Jev had shuttled between visited tiles; the judge put 70 % of the blame on\n  the players, not the rules.\n- the move question states the player''s secret objective and progress.\n- registry: getEnabledMechanics cached by the set of configured keys (it ran\n  on every hook call — ~60 % of engine CPU); simulation cost per decision\n  fell from ~0.57 s to ~0.04 s.\n- devtools/smoke.ts --sim: a free stand-in decider that exercises and times\n  the consequence simulation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011oR3V7hLncLCGgHh8wRUV4\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD/p+PLp\n7m5qGZZYGwG+cbwYg11xegzWd2tYzQCN0sewg5yHdRA09Zi1OsoR3bp4bcxzmb1fyTuk+nh9Bgn4\nNQE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T01:33:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist