47,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/christopherdebeer/workspace/commit/3883e423b650c3ece086870aec64eab1916e10ad","node_id":"C_kwDOORTQmNoAKDM4ODNlNDIzYjY1MGMzZWNlMDg2ODcwYWVjNjRlYWIxOTE2ZTEwYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/christopherdebeer/workspace/commit/c358bd3f5175578a805ccf28d6e9bc659fe8f139","sha":"c358bd3f5175578a805ccf28d6e9bc659fe8f139","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/c358bd3f5175578a805ccf28d6e9bc659fe8f139"}],"sha":"3883e423b650c3ece086870aec64eab1916e10ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/3883e423b650c3ece086870aec64eab1916e10ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/c358bd3f5175578a805ccf28d6e9bc659fe8f139/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T00:54:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T00:54:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"playtest: fan-out evals (one invocation per run); denounce + discovery; outcomes\n\nHarness:\n- evals fan out: a plan classifies once, then every run is its own parallel\n  invocation with the full budget; the run that completes the set assembles\n  the eval (claimed once) and carries out the job (eval / noise / propose\n  decision). The job poll finishes a plan with missing runs as incomplete.\n  A single AAOTE eval had hit the 270 s job budget (one run cut off, scored\n  0.35) and measured noise 0.20 on 6 train games — now suites can grow\n  without the wall clock growing.\n- incomplete evals are never baselines; a round judged on one is reverted as\n  inconclusive without counting toward a stall; an incomplete noise rerun is\n  reported but not stored.\n- harness h3: the judge sees each player''s secret role at the end and names\n  the cause of repetitive play (rules vs players); runs record the winner''s\n  role and how the game ended; evals tally who won as what.\n- consequence simulation never runs moves whose outcome turns on hidden\n  information (denounce, accuse, draw, …); wins shown only when nothing\n  hidden was touched.\n\nEngine (options for rules to use):\n- grid.discover_on_first_visit: N — first entry to any tile draws N cards.\n- hidden_objectives.denounce {correct: win|reveal, wrong: reveal_self|\n  end_turn|both} — once per game, name The Enemy.\n- revealed roles shown to everyone (revealedRoles).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011oR3V7hLncLCGgHh8wRUV4","tree":{"sha":"c777e4f5d4e627e2b2172d02559b65d5f4bdb70d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/trees/c777e4f5d4e627e2b2172d02559b65d5f4bdb70d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/commits/c358bd3f5175578a805ccf28d6e9bc659fe8f139","verification":{"payload":"tree c777e4f5d4e627e2b2172d02559b65d5f4bdb70d\nparent ec587a90f75837680abc79f8d9a7bc9711132d34\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790729666 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790729666 +0000\n\nplaytest: fan-out evals (one invocation per run); denounce + discovery; outcomes\n\nHarness:\n- evals fan out: a plan classifies once, then every run is its own parallel\n  invocation with the full budget; the run that completes the set assembles\n  the eval (claimed once) and carries out the job (eval / noise / propose\n  decision). The job poll finishes a plan with missing runs as incomplete.\n  A single AAOTE eval had hit the 270 s job budget (one run cut off, scored\n  0.35) and measured noise 0.20 on 6 train games — now suites can grow\n  without the wall clock growing.\n- incomplete evals are never baselines; a round judged on one is reverted as\n  inconclusive without counting toward a stall; an incomplete noise rerun is\n  reported but not stored.\n- harness h3: the judge sees each player''s secret role at the end and names\n  the cause of repetitive play (rules vs players); runs record the winner''s\n  role and how the game ended; evals tally who won as what.\n- consequence simulation never runs moves whose outcome turns on hidden\n  information (denounce, accuse, draw, …); wins shown only when nothing\n  hidden was touched.\n\nEngine (options for rules to use):\n- grid.discover_on_first_visit: N — first entry to any tile draws N cards.\n- hidden_objectives.denounce {correct: win|reveal, wrong: reveal_self|\n  end_turn|both} — once per game, name The Enemy.\n- revealed roles shown to everyone (revealedRoles).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.c