open offer means giving an item back; ''accept, give\n  nothing'' let every responder take free items (the Trader won 4/6 games).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011oR3V7hLncLCGgHh8wRUV4","tree":{"sha":"26bfde53a541c341725f3d8aafa1dfd00d9cad03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/trees/26bfde53a541c341725f3d8aafa1dfd00d9cad03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/commits/ae62b422e99bfa043f4f3b71f78df18e7efcd7c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 26bfde53a541c341725f3d8aafa1dfd00d9cad03\nparent c93299bd7ba3f256138a09ef3433de2ef43ea491\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790728720 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790728720 +0000\n\nplaytest: one-ply consequence facts (harness h2); no free items from open offers\n\n- runner: each valid option is played on a throwaway copy of the state and its\n  label gains what visibly changes for the mover — objective progress, score,\n  a win — unless the simulation touched hidden information (deck, others''\n  hands, what the mover learns). Own RNG stream; the slot''s files restored.\n  Jev had been choosing blind (aimless shuttling between two tiles).\n- HARNESS_VERSION is part of an eval''s identity: baselines must match engine,\n  suite, score version and harness (a harness change moves scores without\n  touching engine code).\n- trading: accepting an open offer means giving an item back; ''accept, give\n  nothing'' let every responder take free items (the Trader won 4/6 games).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011oR3V7hLncLCGgHh8wRUV4\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEMFKl9f\nIxB5ppsSQIaeQZF/+oflh5LaYy75JoqdaTCi4ldr52YJVkPgcXd