 1790727202 +0000\n\nplaytest: cell-sync state\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011oR3V7hLncLCGgHh8wRUV4\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCon86T5\npGj/ptZbDz9MvDA2k6lxNYoL7yvBsvYjGUZ3wJA15xpfagy9uI+bjvjsVekxLUKjF8QiuQ0V2Vc7\nHgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T00:13:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/christopherdebeer/workspace/commit/9f3504c4c72a112805ed5a21624d7a0ae071dda6","node_id":"C_kwDOORTQmNoAKDlmMzUwNGM0YzcyYTExMjgwNWVkNWEyMTYyNGQ3YTBhZTA3MWRkYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/christopherdebeer/workspace/commit/18adf327da3abfb2718109b34b4933528ff1e74e","sha":"18adf327da3abfb2718109b34b4933528ff1e74e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/18adf327da3abfb2718109b34b4933528ff1e74e"}],"sha":"9f3504c4c72a112805ed5a21624d7a0ae071dda6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/9f3504c4c72a112805ed5a21624d7a0ae071dda6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/commits/18adf327da3abfb2718109b34b4933528ff1e74e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T00:13:08Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T00:13:08Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"playtest: Jev qualitative critique in every judgement; score/v2\n\nThe judge now reads the prose rules, the whole game round by round (runs\ncollapsed), engine event counts and the classifier''s known engine gaps, and\nrates the session as a designer would on 16 ordered five-step scales: fun,\nengagement, dynamism, tension, meaningful decisions, strategic depth,\ndiversity, interaction, pace, balance, theme, rules coherence, goal clarity,\ncomeback potential, replayability, elegance — plus the biggest weakness,\ngreatest strength and the kind of change that would most improve it.\n\nscore/v2 adds the critique index (mean/4) at .20 (ended .25, judged .15,\nvariety .10, agency .10). Evals aggregate the train critique; the stall\ndiagnosis reports the weakest dimensions and suggested fixes. The page shows\nthe critique on runs and evals, and /api/scoring serves weights and scales.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011oR3V7hLncLCGgHh8wRUV4","tree":{"sha":"af2a3a3efd522a515622aa9c70c6253cca6157a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/trees/af2a3a3efd522a515622aa9c70c6253cca6157a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christopherdebeer/workspace/git/commits/18adf327da3abfb2718109b34b4933528ff1e74e","verification":{"payload":"tree af2a3a3efd522a515622aa9c70c6253cca6157a3\nparent 9ae23494f4aa57a9beb66afd9f13481c9e372ea0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790727188 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790727188 +0000\n\nplaytest: Jev qualitative critique in every judgement; score/v2\n\nThe judge now reads the prose rules, the whole game round by round (runs\ncollapsed), engine event counts and the classifier''s known engine gaps, and\nrates the session as a designer would on 16 ordered five-step scales: fun,\nengagement, dynamism, tension, meaningful decisions, strategic depth,\ndiversity, interaction, pace, balance, theme, rules coherence, goal clarity,\ncomeback potential, replayability, elegance — plus the biggest weakness,\ngreatest strength and the kind of change that would most improve it.\n\nscore/v2 adds the critique index (mean/4) at .20 (ended .25, judged .15,\nvariety .10, agency .10). Evals aggregate the train critique; the stall\ndiagnosis reports the weakest dimensions and suggested fixes. The page shows\nthe critique on runs and evals, and /api/scoring serves weights and scales.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011oR3V7hLncLCGgHh8wRUV4\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEG